{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothAuxiliaryInt","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothAuxiliaryInt","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothAuxiliaryConstruction","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.SiegelsLemma","lean:module:Mathlib.NumberTheory.NumberField.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_prod_lt_card_idxBoxF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_prod_lt_card_idxBoxF","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryInt.lean#L195-L205","doc":"**The counting condition, discharged.**  `deg α · #conditions < #unknowns` from the variance\nargument, in the shape Siegel over `ℤ` consumes.  This is where `m > deg α/(4ε²)` lives — and it is\nthe whole difference between this route and the `house` route, where the degree cancelled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_auxiliary_polynomial_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_auxiliary_polynomial_int","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryInt.lean#L118-L193","doc":"**Route A's step 1.**  A non-zero `ℤ`-coefficient polynomial of bounded degree whose index at\n`(α₁,…,α_m)` is at least `μ`, with Siegel's height bound on its coefficients.\n\n`hcount` is the classical counting condition `deg α · #conditions < #unknowns`; supply it from\n`nsmul_fintypeCard_idxWeight_lt` and `card_chooseBasisIndex_eq_finrank`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.siegelHeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.siegelHeight","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryInt.lean#L104-L116","doc":"**Siegel's height bound for the auxiliary system**, named.\n\nConsumers need to state `Γ_m`'s clauses and the size comparison at the `a` the construction\nactually produces — `⌈siegelHeight⌉` — and not universally over all of `R(a; r)`.  Quantifying\nover every `(P, a)` instead would be a strictly stronger hypothesis and therefore a weaker\ntheorem, and it would ask a caller to check `Γ_m` for polynomials the construction never makes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.auxMatrixInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.auxMatrixInt","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryInt.lean#L94-L102","doc":"The integer matrix of the vanishing conditions.  Rows are pairs (low-weight multi-index,\nintegral-basis coordinate); columns are the box of admissible monomials. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_chooseBasisIndex_eq_finrank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_chooseBasisIndex_eq_finrank","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryInt.lean#L83-L86","doc":"The number of integral-basis coordinates is `deg α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_smul_eq_zero_iff_repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_smul_eq_zero_iff_repr","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryInt.lean#L61-L81","doc":"**One `𝓞 K`-linear condition is `deg α` integer ones.**  The element of `𝓞 K` vanishes exactly\nwhen every coordinate in an integral basis does, and the coordinates of a `ℤ`-combination are the\n`ℤ`-combinations of the coordinates.  This is the step that puts `finrank ℚ K` into the count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.map_ofBox","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.map_ofBox","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothAuxiliaryInt.lean#L47-L53","doc":"`map` commutes with `ofBox`: applying a ring hom to the coefficient vector is applying it to\nthe polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0}]}